<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 16px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Celebrations and Traditions</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> In This Region, They Have a Custom Of...</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Simplify complex text for peers. Text: Mediate everyday instructions to peers.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can simplify for peers a complex text about cultural traditions by using visual aids and encouraging questions (e.g., pointing to a traditional dance picture and saying, "This is a celebration dance. What do you notice about the costumes?"). Can mediate for peers instructions related to cultural events by miming actions (e.g., miming dancing steps for "join the dance"). Can simplify cultural descriptions in texts, using gestures and simple language (e.g., showing a photo and saying, "People wear masks here.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e6f2f9; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e6f2f9; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e6f2f9; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of the mediation skill, connecting to cultural traditions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various images of Panamanian cultural traditions (e.g., Pollera, Diablicos Sucios, Sancocho, parades, tamborito dance). Students are asked to briefly identify them. The teacher then asks, "Imagine your friend from another country doesn't know about this 'parade'. How would you explain it to them so they understand easily?" This introduces the concept of simplifying and mediating information.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher presents a slightly complex sentence about a tradition, e.g., "The Cumbia, traditionally characterized by its intricate footwork and the use of 'tamborito' drums, has been a significant part of our cultural heritage for generations." The teacher then simplifies it: "The Cumbia is a traditional dance. People dance together (teacher mimes dancing). It uses special drums (points to a drum image). It's very old and important to our culture." The teacher emphasizes using simple words, gestures, and visual aids for explaining. The teacher also models pronunciation of words like "cultural" and "celebration."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I simplify something, do I use very difficult words or very easy words?" (Expected: Easy words)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What else can I use to help someone understand, besides just words?" (Expected: Pictures, gestures, miming)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Celebrations and Traditions," focusing on a text that requires mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short informative text (e.g., a paragraph from a tourist brochure or a cultural website) describing a specific Panamanian tradition, such as "La Danza del Diablo" or "El Corpus Christi in La Villa de Los Santos." The text will contain A2.3 level vocabulary (e.g., <i>ritual, ceremony, mask, belief, ancestry</i>) and some slightly complex sentence structures, including present perfect ("People <b>have participated</b> in parades and traditional dances") and gerunds after prepositions ("They are known for <b>wearing</b> colorful masks").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Describing celebrations: "They decorate their homes with the national flag and participate in the parades." Responding to questions: "What traditions are important in your community?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the text individually. Then, they complete:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What is the main tradition described in this text?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False Activity:</b> Students mark sentences about the text as True or False (e.g., "The tradition only happens once a year." "People wear special masks during the festival.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Matching Activity:</b> Students match bolded words from the text (e.g., 'ritual', 'ancestry', 'festive') with simpler definitions or synonyms provided.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on mediating information about cultural traditions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice mediating cultural descriptions and instructions using present simple, past simple, present perfect, and gerunds after prepositions. Focus on vocabulary: <i>tradition, custom, parade, celebration, mask, dance, festival, heritage, observe, traditionally, together</i>. Practice pronunciation of word stress (e.g., "mask," "gather," "cultural," "celebration") and third-person singular verb endings (e.g., "decorates," "gathers," "wishes").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice: Simplify the Sentence.</b> The teacher provides 3-4 slightly complex sentences related to traditions (e.g., "Indigenous communities have consistently preserved their ancestral customs through elaborate ceremonies." or "The annual procession typically culminates in a vibrant display of fireworks and communal gatherings."). Students work individually to rewrite each sentence using simpler language, visual cues (drawing a quick sketch), or gestures they would use to explain it to a peer. Emphasis on gerunds after prepositions (e.g., "You can explain this by <b>showing</b> a picture").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice: Mediate the Instruction.</b> In pairs, students receive cards with common instructions for cultural events (e.g., "Join the dance," "Wear a traditional mask," "Taste the local cuisine," "Observe the ceremony quietly"). One student picks a card and must mediate the instruction to their partner using only simple words, miming, and gestures, without saying the exact phrase. The partner guesses the instruction. They then swap roles. Students practice sounds like /s/ in "decorates" and /z/ in "gathers" when describing actions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction: Explain the Custom.</b> Students return to the initial text from Stage 2. In pairs, one student acts as the "expert" and the other as the "visitor." The expert takes a specific paragraph from the text and simplifies it for their partner, using simple language, gestures, and drawing (if needed). The "visitor" can ask questions like, "What traditions are important in your community?" The expert must use present simple, past simple, and gerunds after prepositions (e.g., "Panama <b>celebrates</b> Fiestas Patrias. It <b>became</b> independent in 1903. Many people <b>have enjoyed</b> going to parades."). They swap roles after mediating one paragraph.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students use the mediation skill in a realistic scenario related to the 21st Century Skills Project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative "Heritage Museum Tour" Presentation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group is assigned a "station" or "exhibit" for their "Heritage Museum Tour" (e.g., "The History of Panamanian Independence," "Traditional Dances of Panama," "Festive Cuisine"). They receive a short, slightly complex text or a set of facts about their assigned topic (which they might have researched in previous lessons). Their task is to prepare a short (2-3 minute) guided tour of their exhibit for another group of "visitors."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">During their tour, they must:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Simplify complex descriptions</b> of traditions or historical facts from their text using simple language, visuals (e.g., pictures, drawings, actual objects if available), and gestures. (e.g., pointing to a picture of a mask and saying, "People wear these masks here. This is a <b>symbol</b> of our <b>ancestry</b>.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Mediate at least two instructions</b> related to cultural events (e.g., "Imagine yourself <b>dancing</b> the tamborito," "You can learn about Panamanian traditions by <b>exploring</b> artifacts," "Join us in <b>celebrating</b> this custom!"). They must use miming or gestures for the instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Respond to at least one question</b> from the "visitors" about their exhibit.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Systematically use target grammar (present simple/past simple for facts, gerunds after prepositions) and vocabulary (<i>tradition, custom, independence, cuisine, parade, celebration, mask, dance, festival, heritage, observe, traditionally, together</i>).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Groups circulate, giving and receiving "tours." The teacher facilitates and observes.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment of students' mediation skills and self-reflection on their learning.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation with a checklist focused on mediation skills and peer feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their "Heritage Museum Tour" to another group. The "visitors" (peers) use a simple checklist to provide feedback to the "tour guides." The teacher observes each group for evidence of the learning outcome.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist & Peer Feedback):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity of Mediation:</b> Did the "tour guides" simplify complex information effectively? (e.g., "The explanation was easy to understand.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Aids:</b> Did they use gestures, miming, or visual aids to help explain?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Target Language:</b> Did they use key vocabulary (e.g., <i>tradition, custom, festival</i>) and grammar (gerunds after prepositions, present simple/past simple)?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Was their pronunciation intelligible, especially word stress and -s/-es/-ies sounds?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Did the group work well together to present their tour?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I did well today to simplify information for my peers was..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Next time I mediate instructions, I will try to use more/better..." (e.g., gestures, simple words, pictures).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Review of the lesson and preparation for future learning.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new thing I learned about communicating information about traditions in a simple way?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I use my mediation skills outside of the classroom?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson to promote mediation skills? (e.g., peer interaction, use of visuals, the museum tour project).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students to further develop their ability to simplify complex texts and mediate instructions? (e.g., more practice with specific types of vocabulary, structured sentence frames for simplification).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson concludes the theme "In This Region, They Have a Custom Of...". The next sequence will introduce a new theme, possibly building on communication skills, but with new vocabulary and contexts, encouraging students to apply their developed language and mediation abilities in diverse scenarios.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>